hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2798","Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-‘Ala’, narrated to us Sufyan, from Yahya, who said: I heard al-Qasim say: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: “Among the Sunnah of Hajj — and he said once: ‘Among the Sunnah of the Imam’ — is that he should pray Zuhr, ‘Asr, Maghrib, ‘Isha’, and Fajr in Muzdalifah.”

---
**CHAPTER:**"
"2799","Narrated to us Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī, narrated to us al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir, narrated to us Abū Kurayb Yaḥyā ibn al-Muhallab al-Bajalī, on the authority of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of al-Ḥakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās (RA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed five prayers in Minā.

**CHAPTER:**"
